{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK7Su76JejJRK9WBqwxo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The autoreloader now watches `manage.py`, so editing it triggers a reload again.\n\nWhen Django is started with `python manage.py runserver`, the `__main__` module has no `__spec__`. `iter_modules_and_files()` in `django/utils/autoreload.py` skipped any module without one, so `manage.py` was never watched. It now treats `__main__` as a special case and uses its `__file__` instead.\n\nI ran the existing `utils_tests.test_autoreload` module and it passes (21 skipped). I didn't add a test for the `__main__` case, and I didn't start a real `runserver` to watch the reload happen."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":994,"cache_read_input_tokens":20013,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":994},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b655f7b-8d67-420a-8c78-2dbce41f82a0","uuid":"2ee6b0f5-591a-4845-9b02-b69a237f4c89","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:59:36.801Z","request_id":"req_011ChK7StyQzbYf4Wp1sD7E8"}
